{
  "id":"design-key-value-store","version":1,"title":"Design a Key-Value Store","difficulty":"Intermediate",
  "scenario":"Build a key-value API that serves 600 requests per second, half gets and half puts, over 96 keys. The datastore begins with seeded values. A correct get returns the current value; a put persists its new value. You may use explicit load balancing, caching, and separate read/write routes. All component instances count toward the budget.",
